# One canonical line ending for the whole repository.
#
# WHY. Without this file, git honours each developer's local
# core.autocrlf. On Windows that is `true` by default, so text files are
# materialised with CRLF while the repository stores LF. Any test that
# asserts a file's exact bytes — for example the robots.txt content
# assertion in tests/Feature/Website/Public/WebsiteIndexingTest.php —
# then passes on Linux CI and fails on every Windows checkout, for a
# reason that has nothing to do with the code under test.
#
# `eol=lf` makes the working tree match the repository on every platform,
# so "the bytes on disk" means the same thing everywhere.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Platform-specific scripts and project files that Windows tooling
# requires — or strongly expects — to be CRLF. The global rule above must
# never reach them. None of these are tracked today; they are declared up
# front so the first one added cannot be silently corrupted on checkout.
#
#   *.bat/*.cmd  cmd.exe mis-parses a multi-line LF batch file, most
#                visibly around labels and `goto`.
#   *.reg        regedit rejects a .reg file that is not CRLF.
#   *.ps1 etc.   Authenticode signature blocks are line-ending sensitive.
#   MSBuild/VS   .sln and *proj files are rewritten as CRLF by the IDE,
#                so LF guarantees a diff on every save.
*.bat      text eol=crlf
*.cmd      text eol=crlf
*.reg      text eol=crlf
*.ps1      text eol=crlf
*.psm1     text eol=crlf
*.psd1     text eol=crlf
*.vbs      text eol=crlf
*.sln      text eol=crlf
*.csproj   text eol=crlf
*.vbproj   text eol=crlf
*.vcxproj  text eol=crlf
*.props    text eol=crlf
*.targets  text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touched, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.svgz binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
*.eot binary
*.otf binary
*.mp3 binary
*.mp4 binary
*.xlsx binary

# Better diffs for the languages this repository actually contains.
*.php diff=php
*.blade.php diff=html
*.css diff=css
*.scss diff=css
*.html diff=html
*.md diff=markdown
